<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 2 May, from 1194 to 1972.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1194">1194 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">832 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard I grants Portsmouth its first royal charter</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a> gave Portsmouth its first royal charter, establishing it as a town. The settlement had been founded around 1180 by the Anglo-Norman merchant Jean de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gisors">Gisors</a> on Portsea Island.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1250">1250 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">776 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mamluks under Baybars murder the Ayyubid sultan Turanshah</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> murdered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turanshah">Turanshah</a>, Ayyubid sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> since 1249, for fear of losing their privileges. That year the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a> was overthrown in Egypt by its own mamluk soldiers, who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1519">1519 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">507 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Leonardo da Vinci dies at Amboise</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Leonardo died at Clos Lucé, the manor near Amboise given to him by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a>. Painter of the Mona Lisa and The Last Supper, he also left thousands of pages of notes on anatomy, engineering and nature.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1536">1536 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">490 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Anne Boleyn is arrested and taken to the Tower</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Queen Anne Boleyn was arrested at Greenwich on charges of adultery, incest and treason. She was beheaded at the Tower seventeen days later, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> married Jane Seymour within days.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1670">1670 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">356 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles II charters the Hudson's Bay Company</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The company received a monopoly of trade across the lands draining into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-bay">Hudson Bay</a>, a vast territory named Rupert's Land. It remains one of the oldest commercial enterprises in the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudson-bay">Hudson Bay</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1808">1808 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">218 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Madrid rises against French occupation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Crowds in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a> attacked French troops in the Dos de Mayo uprising, which was suppressed with mass executions painted by Goya. Revolt spread across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peninsular-war">Peninsular War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peninsular-war">Peninsular War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1863">1863 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stonewall Jackson is shot by his own men at Chancellorsville</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Returning from a night reconnaissance, General Thomas 'Stonewall' Jackson was hit by fire from Confederate pickets. He died of pneumonia eight days later, a grave loss to Lee.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Berlin garrison surrenders to the Red Army</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General Helmuth Weidling surrendered the German forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> to the Soviets two days after Hitler's suicide. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s unconditional surrender followed within a week.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1972">1972 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">54 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">J. Edgar Hoover dies after 48 years leading the FBI</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">J. Edgar Hoover died in Washington, having led the Bureau and its predecessor since 1924. He built a modern federal police force but also used it to spy on activists and politicians.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 2 May <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rene-ii-duke-of-lorraine"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rene-ii-duke-of-lorraine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">René II, Duke of Lorraine</span><span class="tp">1451–1508</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jigme-dorji-wangchuck"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jigme-dorji-wangchuck.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jigme Dorji Wangchuck</span><span class="tp">1929–1972</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/faisal-ii-of-iraq"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/faisal-ii-of-iraq.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Faisal II of Iraq</span><span class="tp">1935–1958</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/moshoeshoe-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/moshoeshoe-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Moshoeshoe II</span><span class="tp">1938–1996</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 2 May <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leo-i-king-of-armenia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leo-i-king-of-armenia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leo I, King of Armenia</span><span class="tp">1150–1219</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/franz-von-papen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/franz-von-papen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Franz von Papen</span><span class="tp">1879–1969</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/osama-bin-laden"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/osama-bin-laden.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Osama bin Laden</span><span class="tp">1957–2011</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
